            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to pass the entrance exam for, then the Mandarin for to fail an entrance exam."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 期中",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "期中 — qīzhōng — \"the middle of the term; midterm\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zhè cì qīzhōng kǎoshì wǒ gǎnjué hái xíng — I think this midterm went all right."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "期中 (qīzhōng) is built from 期 'a set time' and 中 'the middle', both inherited from Middle Chinese, gi and trjuwng (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'an appointed time'. The modern first tone of qī is irregular: gi would regularly give qí."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying how it was."
