          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "考场 — kǎochǎng — \"exam hall; exam room\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "进考场以前我喝了一杯水 jìn kǎochǎng yǐqián wǒ hē le yì bēi shuǐ — Before going into the exam hall, I drank a glass of water."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two third tones meet in this word: kǎo is said with a rising tone before chǎng, and the spelling keeps both marks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "考场 (kǎochǎng) is built from 考 'to examine' and 场 'a ground', both inherited from Middle Chinese, khawX and drjang (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second 'a threshing floor'; the third tone of chǎng is irregular for drjang."
            }
          ]
        },
